#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087475 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9be02ade-3dd2-5ec3-a532-78d1151dc89f" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Complex Number Shown on an Argand Diagram in Exponential Form"}] :question/id #uuid "73491cdd-3c8c-5203-b403-6176f6eb2917" :question/math-academy-id "e-5280" :question/problem "Write the complex number $z$, shown in the following Argand diagram, in exponential form.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/898/Source/Images/a0fe46e109e3784d66675d033d5fdbd8.png)" :question/worked-solution "The complex number shown in the Argand diagram can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nz &= x + \\textrm{i}y \\\\\n&=-3 + 2\\textrm{i}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo write it in the form\n\n$$\nz = r\\textrm{e}^{\\textrm{i}\\theta}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nr= \\mid z \\mid\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\theta = \\arg(z)\n$$\n\nwe first calculate $r$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr = \\mid z \\mid &= \\sqrt{x^{2} + y^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{(-3)^{2} + 2^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{13}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $z$ lies in the second quadrant, we can find the angle $\\theta$ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\arg (z) &= π - \\mid \\arctan (\\frac{y}{x}) \\mid \\\\\n&= π - \\mid \\arctan (\\frac{2}{3}) \\mid \\\\\n&= π - 0.588 \\\\\n&= 2.554\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nto three decimal places.\n\nFinally, substituting\n\n$$\nr=\\sqrt{13}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\theta=2.554\n$$\n\ninto\n\n$$\nz=re^{\\textrm{i} \\theta}\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\nz = \\sqrt{13}\\,\\textrm{e}^{2.554\\,\\textrm{i}}\\,\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087476 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "01caf021-de3e-5e2a-89ce-ba289b65c0ff" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Complex Number in Exponential Form"}] :question/id #uuid "339f9406-2f1a-52de-959b-23a7fe73ef68" :question/math-academy-id "e-5282" :question/problem "Write the complex number $z=4+4\\textrm{i}$ in exponential form." :question/worked-solution "To write our complex number in the form\n\n$$\nz = r\\textrm{e}^{\\textrm{i}\\theta}\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\nr= \\mid z \\mid\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\theta = \\arg(z)\n$$\n\nwe first calculate $r$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nr = \\mid z \\mid &= \\sqrt{x^{2} + y^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{4^{2} + 4^{2}} \\\\\n&= 4\\sqrt{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $z$ lies in the first quadrant of the complex plane, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nθ = \\arg (z) &= \\arctan (\\frac{y}{x}) \\\\\n&= \\arctan (1) \\\\\n&= \\frac{π}{4}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting\n\n$$\nr=4\\sqrt{2}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\theta=\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\n$$\n\ninto\n\n$$\nz=re^{\\textrm{i}\\theta}\n$$\n\nwe get\n\n$$\nz = 4\\sqrt{2}\\,\\textrm{e}^{\\pi\\textrm{i}/4}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186277519 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9be02ade-3dd2-5ec3-a532-78d1151dc89f" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Complex Number Shown on an Argand Diagram in Exponential Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "90584326-4b33-57bc-80d2-a8018dd5851f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{13}\\,{\\text{e}}^{5.3\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277521} {:answer/id #uuid "df9c597d-d8ac-56dd-b725-4de35d2a5554" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{13}\\,{\\text{e}}^{4.8\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277522} {:answer/id #uuid "f83c4ac3-3150-5969-922e-65e28006235c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{11}\\,{\\text{e}}^{4.8\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277523} {:answer/id #uuid "ac65ced2-49e1-5c54-afc6-1048b69aae55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{11}\\,{\\text{e}}^{5.3\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277524} {:answer/id #uuid "0fa4696f-b63e-5d00-9f16-8cf7f8057351" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{13}\\,{\\text{e}}^{4.1\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277525}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "90584326-4b33-57bc-80d2-a8018dd5851f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{13}\\,{\\text{e}}^{5.3\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277521} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5aad4bf-4ff8-5f2d-bb23-efadfc58c28c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277520}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "98e9dda0-b7c6-5b8c-836e-5f373b899981" :question/math-academy-id "q-107428" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973361/assets/ba77669a8e0ffd3e69bfc8e5322d7042c318a55b4cd486ac1fac591d3b016e43.png)\n\nWrite the complex number $z$, shown on the Argand diagram above, in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ giving $\\theta $ in radians to the nearest tenth." :question/worked-solution "The complex number shown in the Argand diagram can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =x+\\text{i}y \\\\  & =2-3\\,\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo write it in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{2}^{2}+(-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{13}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $z$ lies in the fourth quadrant, we can find the angle $\\theta $ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =2\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =2\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{3}{2})| \\\\  & ≈5.3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=\\sqrt{13}$ and $\\theta =5.3$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get \n\n$$\nz=\\sqrt{13}\\,{\\text{e}}^{5.3\\,\\text{i}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087998 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9be02ade-3dd2-5ec3-a532-78d1151dc89f" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Complex Number Shown on an Argand Diagram in Exponential Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0314343c-79ca-52be-87a6-a7908c491b93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z = 5e^{2π\\textrm{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085000} {:answer/id #uuid "27903711-eed5-5c4e-8424-7ae9fad03fbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z = 5e^{0.464\\textrm{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085001} {:answer/id #uuid "35ca178d-953f-5a01-a340-d00e705dc593" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z = \\sqrt{5}e^{1.644\\textrm{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085002} {:answer/id #uuid "4dacd689-bf24-5744-83ac-73bc89a7abc3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z = 5e^{0.644\\textrm{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085003} {:answer/id #uuid "6d9a94f0-37ce-5ff6-ace9-a00ad67f61a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z = \\sqrt{5}e^{0.644\\textrm{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085004}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4dacd689-bf24-5744-83ac-73bc89a7abc3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z = 5e^{0.644\\textrm{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186085003} :answer-field/id #uuid "e3186540-f6c7-5400-bfaf-d4ce2a08e425" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186084999}] :question/id #uuid "41ba3c7b-634a-5f48-9b9b-3e5652d0eb21" :question/math-academy-id "q-17517" :question/problem "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/898/Source/Images/q-17517.png)\n\nWrite the complex number $z$, shown on the Argand diagram above, in the form $re^{\\textrm{i}θ}$, giving $θ$ in radians to three decimal places." :question/requires-calculator true}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338272 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "01caf021-de3e-5e2a-89ce-ba289b65c0ff" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Complex Number in Exponential Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9284b0a5-6797-5f77-b7a1-d4c0b8fe315e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=2\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.389\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338274} {:answer/id #uuid "027c16c5-2973-5717-8af4-0135a10f6020" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=2\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338275} {:answer/id #uuid "76927f0f-078b-5d44-88fa-aa29a676241c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=2\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.893\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338276} {:answer/id #uuid "274fc05d-1f82-55d1-bec8-b925b6291c70" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338277} {:answer/id #uuid "42cfe6cd-8c70-5046-b98e-d974d4d8aea6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=2\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.983\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338278}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "76927f0f-078b-5d44-88fa-aa29a676241c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=2\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.893\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338276} :answer-field/id #uuid "e5df713a-1952-5f2f-aad9-fbc435f9cd6a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186338273}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7a435c59-9a38-57a4-9c2b-af498b51b708" :question/math-academy-id "q-17524" :question/problem "Write the complex number $z=-2+6\\text{i}$ in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ giving $\\theta $ in radians to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "To write our complex number in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2)^{2}+{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =2\\sqrt{10}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $z$ lies in the second quadrant of the complex plane, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-3)| \\\\  & ≈1.893.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=2\\sqrt{10}$ and $\\theta =1.893$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=2\\sqrt{10}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.893\\,\\text{i}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088231 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9be02ade-3dd2-5ec3-a532-78d1151dc89f" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Complex Number Shown on an Argand Diagram in Exponential Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93831ade-92f3-55a1-898c-1fa9b3e39dc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z = 2\\sqrt{3}e^{π\\textrm{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086318} {:answer/id #uuid "ba7fafd2-561e-57cf-b458-6ac7b266706e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z = 2e^{5π\\textrm{i}/6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086319} {:answer/id #uuid "12a1c4f6-c394-5811-bf5c-ec8f6641bd82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z = 3e^{3π\\textrm{i}/4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086320} {:answer/id #uuid "2c382927-796b-5057-a3b3-9cad5a5084cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z = 3\\sqrt{2}e^{π\\textrm{i}/6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086321} {:answer/id #uuid "363041ed-687c-5519-803b-30905ceab477" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z = 2e^{2π\\textrm{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086322}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "363041ed-687c-5519-803b-30905ceab477" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z = 2e^{2π\\textrm{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086322} :answer-field/id #uuid "1736925a-0723-5e18-b493-5324e70cc51b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086317}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "145945c1-66ab-5fe7-89d2-3b7864c48fb7" :question/math-academy-id "q-71978" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14059847/assets/c5d36b72e7e2ff6754152a559d64bf3610708c9a2d3790c859bc9abacc9220b6.png)\n\nWrite the complex number $z$, shown on the Argand diagram above, in exponential form." :question/requires-calculator true :question/worked-solution "The complex number shown in the Argand diagram can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}z & =x+\\text{i}y \\\\  & =-1+\\sqrt{3}\\,\\text{i}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo write it in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-1)^{2}+{(\\sqrt{3})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4} \\\\  & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $z$ lies in the second quadrant, we can find the angle $\\theta $ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\sqrt{3})| \\\\  & =\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=2$ and $\\theta =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=2\\,{\\text{e}}^{2\\pi \\text{i}/3}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088232 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "01caf021-de3e-5e2a-89ce-ba289b65c0ff" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Complex Number in Exponential Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9a422909-dd85-55e4-8d4f-c695dcb437fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z = \\sqrt{2}e^{3π\\textrm{i}/4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086324} {:answer/id #uuid "a4ec03a7-6451-5e1b-8088-ac255fc6641f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z = \\sqrt{2}e^{2π\\textrm{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086325} {:answer/id #uuid "eb5693d5-e031-5535-a904-8965d2485327" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z = 2e^{2π\\textrm{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086326} {:answer/id #uuid "fc2991aa-4826-58b3-859e-86db4b3a25cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z = 2e^{5π\\textrm{i}/6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086327} {:answer/id #uuid "664803c1-ea79-503b-879e-b207d72a6361" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z = \\sqrt{2}e^{5π\\textrm{i}/6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086328}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a422909-dd85-55e4-8d4f-c695dcb437fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z = \\sqrt{2}e^{3π\\textrm{i}/4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086324} :answer-field/id #uuid "78c8484e-d1df-5f93-a17d-97780d4f325f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186086323}] :question/id #uuid "8d71971a-ef79-5e9d-a922-8354775291f8" :question/math-academy-id "q-71983" :question/problem "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nWrite the complex number $z =-1 + \\textrm{i}$ in exponential form." :question/requires-calculator true}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186277533 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "01caf021-de3e-5e2a-89ce-ba289b65c0ff" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Complex Number in Exponential Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5239242c-fdf3-5e96-a7e8-45892f453bac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.107\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277535} {:answer/id #uuid "717617e5-3233-5d91-88b6-89e70771a06a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277536} {:answer/id #uuid "0e112f63-cff3-51b1-9145-10c9df578f79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{0.817\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277537} {:answer/id #uuid "4a4a8597-e154-56ed-91d6-9041fe03a02d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{\\pi \\text{i}/3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277538} {:answer/id #uuid "0df0e5d1-3a63-5f80-8f27-936ecc2d1aca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{3}\\,{\\text{e}}^{0.456\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277539}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5239242c-fdf3-5e96-a7e8-45892f453bac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.107\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277535} :answer-field/id #uuid "0dc6721c-942b-511f-9324-3b1411fc3665" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277534}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "087bd2ce-cf81-51d6-811a-35d764be7f1b" :question/math-academy-id "q-8075" :question/problem "Write the complex number $z=1+2\\text{i}$ in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ giving $\\theta $ in radians to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "To write $z$ in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $z$ lies in the first quadrant of the complex plane, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{2}{1}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(2) \\\\  & ≈1.107.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=\\sqrt{5}$ and $\\theta =1.107$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=\\sqrt{5}\\,{\\text{e}}^{1.107\\,\\text{i}}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186266096 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "01caf021-de3e-5e2a-89ce-ba289b65c0ff" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Complex Number in Exponential Form"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6c49e3d4-1141-5e86-9dc0-07a769f8d693" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{26}\\,{\\text{e}}^{6.086\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266098} {:answer/id #uuid "6b55a12f-e52a-5d98-84d6-20878083f7be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{26}\\,{\\text{e}}^{3.338\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266099} {:answer/id #uuid "32aa2e4b-9f77-5cb7-8958-e69543136db6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{26}\\,{\\text{e}}^{4.989\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266100} {:answer/id #uuid "4c394217-aa5e-5f73-8b5a-b6cc3654b8ac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{17}\\,{\\text{e}}^{6.086\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266101} {:answer/id #uuid "f92c6ec2-5174-5770-b4fe-0716b26824e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{17}\\,{\\text{e}}^{3.338\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266102}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6c49e3d4-1141-5e86-9dc0-07a769f8d693" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "z=\\sqrt{26}\\,{\\text{e}}^{6.086\\,\\text{i}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266098} :answer-field/id #uuid "e293d670-8dd1-5590-974c-860db0453b5a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186266097}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "de095b2a-fbb0-51f2-b405-5336c443d2b4" :question/math-academy-id "q-8076" :question/problem "Write the complex number $z=5-\\text{i}$ in the form $r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ giving $\\theta $ in radians to $3$ decimal places." :question/worked-solution "To write our complex number in the form $z=r{\\text{e}}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ where $r=|z|$ and $\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z),$ we first calculate $r:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r=|z| & =\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{5}^{2}+(-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{26}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $z$ lies in the fourth quadrant, we can find the angle $\\theta $ as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta =\\operatorname{arg}⁡(z) & =2\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{y}{x})| \\\\  & =2\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{-1}{5})| \\\\  & =2\\pi -|\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(-\\frac{1}{5})| \\\\  & ≈2\\pi -0.197\\,39… \\\\  & ≈6.086.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting $r=\\sqrt{26}$ and $\\theta =6.086$ into $z=r{e}^{\\text{i}\\theta },$ we get\n\n$$\nz=\\sqrt{26}\\,{\\text{e}}^{6.086\\,\\text{i}}.\n$$"}]}
